      <h2>Useful Sinhala Phrases for Eating</h2>

      <p><strong>Mama bat kanna one</strong> — I want to eat rice and curry.<br/>
      <strong>Karavadda næhæ</strong> — Not spicy, please.<br/>
      <strong>Eka kiyada?</strong> — How much is this?<br/>
      <strong>Bill eka genna</strong> — Please bring the bill.<br/>
      <strong>Bohoma rasai</strong> — Very delicious.</p>

      <p>A knowledge of even a few words is received with warmth. Sri Lankans are proud of their food and genuinely pleased when visitors make the effort to eat local.</p>

